"Any way to tell if a drive or controller is LVD as opposed to SE?" 
Some drives are explicitly labeled as LVD or SE or both (as with Seagate 
LVD/SE).  If not explicitly labeled, you need to get the specs for the 
manufacturer and model of the drive or controller.  Fortunately, the 
specs for the major SCSI HBAs and drives remain on line at the mfr's web 
sites.  Exceptions may be where product lines were acquired by another 
company.  BusTek/BusLogic SCSI HBAs have a long and tortured trail of 
ownership, first by Mylex, then by IBM, and maybe now by LSI, who have 
gathered together a lot of SCSI products and intellectual property under 
one roof... Ben Myers



