Right.  However, faster disks (at least Ultra) will work in a grey,
BA356 though presumably at the slower speed.  (AFAIK the general rule is 
that when mixing speeds, widths etc everything will work, though at the 
speed of the slowest component, except that a wide disk in a narrow 
shelf won't work.  This refers to the chain controller-cable-shelf-disk.
Disks of different speeds should work at their own speed if the rest of 
the chain supports it, i.e. one slow disk won't slow others down, though 
one SE disk will force all disks on the bus to work in SE mode.)

