There is a manual for the DS-BA35X-FB series. It is very detailed but
not intended as a tutorial.
The DS-BA35X-FB operates in several modes. From memory, it can drive:
  one BA350 cabinet, disk (or tape) SCSI id's are in the range 0..6
(7 reserved for the DS-BA35X-FB)
  one BA350 cabinet in split bus mode
  two BA350 cabinets, disk SCSI id's in the range 0..6 and 8..15.
On top of the DS-BA35X-FB there are two banks of switches. One has
just two and these control termination.
The other has 8 switches and these control split-bus mode, the number
of cabinets attached.
If you can't find the manual on-line then I'll mail it to you (I'm at
work right now and my own systems are all down).
Hans


