------

Prior to V8.4 both a USB keyboard and mouse need to be plugged in for 
DECwindows to start (30 second timeout wait).  The need for a KB/Mouse has 
always been present - but masked by the fact that prior to USB the 
"controllers" for them always showed up even if the devices might not be 
plugged in.  In V8.4 and forward, if there is graphics, and you have 
installed DECwindows and not disabled graphics... then DECwindows will start 
and you can plug in a KB/Mouse any time you want (even more than one of 
each).

Any random USB keyboard should work on VMS.  You can even program 
translation tables for ones that don't look like a VMS or "standard" 
(Windows/UNIX) keyboard.





