You don't enter anything in the AlphaBIOS setup except to select the
OS type and then restart- no need to enter (or point in entering) Boot
Path, OS file, options, etc. The "OS selection" stuff in AlphaBIOS
only applies to OSes booted via AlphaBIOS (NT, some Linux). Or maybe I
should call it the ARC Console rather than AlphaBIOS, can't
remember...

"CMOS Setup" (advanced) was certainly the screen I was thinking of,
but I couldn't remember the exact name.

My first draft earlier (which was lost due to 1d1ot error) mentioned
checking/replacing your battery, as Michael has also mentioned,
otherwise you probably repeat this exercise every power on.

If you should feel inclined to revert to AlphaBIOS, ">>> set os_type
NT" is what I remember as the relevant incantation. Afaik there is no
equally simple route to go the other way - you have to navigate menus.


