> do I need two power supplies in a shelf (and do I need 131W or 150W)?

Phillip,
this is a bit of a SWAG but the KZPSA was probably mostly used in
systems that were part of a SCSI cluster.
IIRC the KZPSA has only one internal connector. Several Alpha models
supported split bus for the internal disk bays.
So the KZPAC Mylex DAC960 controllers (one channel or three channels)
and the KZPCM (two channels plus ethernet on board) were
probably a better choice for those systems. The KZPCM supports ultra
wide SCSI, the Mylex is a RAID controller.

There was also a KZPBA (IIRC), a single channel Qlogic 1040
controller.
Hans


