Here's a list (not exhaustive, but most systems mentioned) of the SCSI 
adapters Alphas:

DEC3000:

Integrated; SCSI-1 narrow SE
PMAZ-A, PMAZ-B, PMAZ-C; SCSI-1 (5MB/s, narrow, SE)
KZTSA-AA; SCSI-2 FWD

DEC4000:

Integrated; SCSI-1 narrow SE

AlphaServers (PCI bus unless otherwise noted):

Integrated;  (AS300, AS400, DEC2000) FNSE, (AS1000, AS2000, AS2100) 
FWSE, (AS800) UWSE

KZPSA; SCSI-2 FWD (HVD)
KZPDA; SCSI-2 SE
KZPAA-AA; SCSI-2 SE (narrow)
KZPBA-CA (-CX); Ultra SE
KZPBA-CB (-CY); Ultra FWD (HVD)
KZPCM; Dual Channel Ultra SE (+ 10/100 Ethernet)
KZPCA-AA; Ultra2 LVD
KZPEA-DB; Dual Channel Ultra3 (Ultra160) LVD/SE

RAID Adapters:

KZESC; SCSI-2 FWSE (EISA bus)
KZPSC; SCSI-2 FWSE
KZPAC; Ultra SE
KZPBC; Ultra SE
KZPCC; Ultra2 LVD (1/3 Channels)
KZPDC; Ultra3 LVD (2/4 Channels)

AlphaStations with integrated adapters:

AXP150; FNSE
AS200, AS255; FNSE
AS500, AS600; FWSE
PWS; UWSE
XP1000; UWSE


The BA35* Enclosures have the following capabilities:

BA353; SCSI-1 NSE (5MB/s)
BA350; FNSE (up to 10MB/s)
BA356 (grey); FWSE (up to 20MB/s)
BA356 (blue); UWSE (up to 40MB/s)

Depending on the Personality module, the external bus can be FNSE, FWSE 
or UWSE and even UWD (HVD).
The internal bus can be a single or dual bus depending on the 
combination of jumper/terminator board and the Personality Module.

There are four different power supply models;

BA35X�HA, AC, 130W (grey); used with the BA350 and older devices (=< 
RZ28, IIRC)
BA35X�HF, AC, 150W (grey); used with the BA356 or BA350
BA35X�HG, DC, 150W (grey); used with the BA356 or BA350
BA35X�HH, DC, 180W (blue); used with BA356 Ultra (blue) enclosures.

The power supplies are capable of handling a fully populated enclosure. 
The second power supply is for redundancy.


Hope this is of any help.

Kari



