John, page B-3 also reports that the FRU is the system module.
There's no information in the entire manual which might indicate that
the main board is dead.
To identify the problem, you might want to remove as much components
as possible: all memory,
disconnect disks and tapes and put the S3 switch in serial mode. If
the result is the same then
perhaps the power supply is at fault, so swapping power supplies might
show a difference.
If not then the main board has a fault somewhere I do not know how you
could narrow that down.
The phrase "...but no instruction has been run" seems to indicate the
VAX processor is at fault.
It is not a badly terminated ethernet nor a dead battery. In those
cases you get an extended error message on the console;
from your description I understand that the console (a VT420) remains
black.
Hans


