There'll be a small socketed chip for Ethernet ID (MAC address) on
there somewhere so that the system can retain the same MAC address if
the main board is swapped (take ID chip out of old board, put in new
board, new system ID is same as old system was). Now, anyone want to
guess what ENET ADRS on this chip might mean? Removing and reseating
it is unlikely to magically make the system work again :(


