I finally figured out my silly problem.

I ran xmodmap to change shift-comma to the less than sign and 
shift-period to the greater than sign.  No change.  Shift key still had 
no effect on those two keys.  I knew I must have had it right since I 
found several examples on the net to do exactly that.

I then remembered/noticed the Options/Keyboard menu on the DECterm 
window.  Sure enough, there's an option to choose what 
shift-period/shift comma do. I selected the shift=angle bracket option and
it now works correctly.  So for DECterms that option overrides what 
xmodmap says.  And I wasn't trying it with non-DECterms.

I guess it's been too long, that's been there since the '90s, and
I supposedly knew about it.



