On 2010-10-28, JohnF <john@please.see.sig.for.email.com> wrote:
>
> I'm not sure if a C program with something like
> unsigned char *imageaddr = 12345;
> would point to an absolute address or just get relocated
> at link/run time.

It would point to an absolute address; the problem is that V stands for 
virtual. You need to either run on the bare hardware (with the MMU off)
or arrange for a mapping to cover the physical address space you want to
talk to. For VMS, that involves creating a PFN mapping. I'm not sure
how to do it in NetBSD.
-- 
