The Smart Array is a RAID controller, yes. There are two versions 5302A 
(KZPDC-BE) and 5304A (KZPDC-DF). The former is the 2 channel verion and 
the latter the 4 channel version.

In the configuration list, it shows up e.g. like

 >>> show config
	.
	.
	.
	.
Compaq/HP Smart Array 5300A pya0.0.0.7.2
	.
	.
	.


If and when there are logical disks defined in the Smart Array 
controller, they'll show up as:

dya1.0.0.9.0 CPQCISS
dya2.0.0.9.0 CPQCISS
dya0.0.0.9.0 CPQCISS

They act as other disks and can even be boot devices. In that case you 
have to set parameters in SRM.

There is a configuration utility residing on the adapter which you can 
run from SRM (if the needed SRM variables are set) by issuing:

 >>> run bios pya0

The menu based configuration utility will then show up and you can view 
and modify the configuration.

There's information about it:
http://www.compaq.com/alphaserver/products/storage/sa5300a/index.html



