Phillip, my attempt to make a table with just blanks failed miserably
I'm afraid.
Your conclusions were all correct though. An Alpha Server 1200 (and
thus a Digital Server 5305 too)
draws 72 Watts with both mains plugs connected and the power switch in
the off position.
I have 6 of them, connected to a mains socket so I now understand why
my annual energy consumption
is more than 7200 kWhr.
A couple of power strips with an on/off switch were a good investment.
They are about =804 or so.
A modern PC and a 15 year old VAXstation draw the same amount of
power, switched on and switched off.
The Alpha Server 1200 was intended for a machine room and are
generally always switched on 24/24 and
possibly the power supplies for these systems follow a different
design.
Or may be the lifespan of equipment improves significantly when more
components are kept power on.
I have all my systems now behind power strips and switched off when
not in use. If suddenly equipment starts
to fail I'll let you know.
Hans


