On the DS10, the NVRAM doesn't contain settings. It contains a "script"
file called "nvram" which has SRM commands which are executed during
power up.

You need to edit this file and change lines that set the console. (or
add one).

the "console" variable defaults to "graphic" (or graphics , not sure)

So if your nvram file contains a set console graphics command, you need
to replace it with set console serial. And if your nvram file contains
no command to set the console, you need to add a line to set the console
to serial


