Console V5.9-1 Dec 14 2000 16:19:05

CPU 0 booting

>>>
>>>^C
>>>^C
>>>^C
>>>^C
>>>^C
>>>show console
console                 serial
>>>

   There's a delay between the (frantic) Ctrl/C hitting and
the visible response.  For all I know, one well-timed Ctrl/C
would do the job, but I normally wait for "CPU 0 booting",
then hit Ctrl/C many times, and then I wait, and hope that I
got it in time.  If it actually starts to boot, then Ctrl/P
may be effective, but I try not to let it get that far.  In
general, it's the same story as at the PS/2 keyboard when the
console is set to graphics.


