Sometimes, this is even suggested by the console itself (e.g. "error 
occurred, retrying, type Ctrl/C to abort).

> Ctrl/P may be a VMS
> thing.  

On some machines, it is the equivalent of the physical switch to get to 
the console (e.g. the response to "use console to halt system" after a 
shutdown).

> Ctrl/X seems to do something like toggle the console
> between graphics and serial.  (I probably discovered that one
> by accident, mistyping Ctrl/C.)

Maybe the equivalent of the S3 switch.



