Thisis one of the most frustrating things I've
found in working with an Alpha workstation:
the absence of a physical HALT button/switch.

I've got a DPWS 600au, and at least I can hit
the "interrupt" button early in the boot to get
to the console, but...

My recommendation is that while you're in
the midst of configuring this beast, set
Auto_Action to HALT and only change
back to RESTART after you're happy with
everything.  Once you have the system
the way you want it, a normal boot followed
by a SHUTDOWN with the NoReboot
option (and no poweroff) will get you to the
console during the odd times you need it.

    -Ken

P.S. Anyone know if the Ctrl/C or Ctrl/X
       trick works on a 600au?  I never
       thought to try that one!


