Well just to be clear (and not sitting in front of
the 600au), on the upper left of the front panel,
there is a power button and what I term an
"interrupt" or "reset" button, which is momentary,
it doesn't stay engaged.

In contrast, the old Alpha 4100's have three
buttons: 2-position power, 2-position halt in
the middle (with an inverted-triangle-in-circle
symbol), and momentary interrupt/reset on
the right.  With the halt button in, the boot
halts at the console prompt after completing
the POST and initialization sequences.

    Regards, Ken


