Phillip,
there are at least two BA356 manuals online (bitsavers probably). If
you can't find them the I'll mail them to you.
They explain in fine detail how to configure the BA356-xx adapters.
An SBB with a SCSI connector, there are two different options:
(1) a DWZZA or DWZZB, these convert one SCSI flavor to another
(2) it is a DSSI-to-SCSI converter, wasn't that called HSD-10?
My systems have KZPCM-Dx boards, they're single ended. To build a SCSI
cluster you need differential scsi boards, such as the KZPSA-xx
adapter. I try to stick to the single ended devices, if only to avoid
damage to disks and/or controllers...
With my limited experience at home I'd say that cables are not
specific to HVD, LVD devices, they obviously make a difference for
wide and narrow devices. The length of the cable is very likely more
of an issue. Faster speeds usually mean shorter cables.
Won't the Systems & Options guides provide information on that? Or
else the manuals that come with the controllers?
Hans
Hans


